Parity: web components/ai/AIFeatureCard.tsx (+ AIBadge, AiOutputPanel, AIThinkingIndicator, HelixMark).
Composition: reusable scaffold - GlassPanel > header(title + cyan Helix badge + description + optional emptyHint)
  > optional inputSlot > Ask-Helix action(inline/below placement) > optional children > output panel.
States reproduced: Hidden/Ready(empty), Thinking(loading), Content, Error(+retry), Stale(refreshing chip + last text),
  Offline(cached + chip). Action label flips Ask Helix <-> Helix is thinking; disabled while busy/offline/not-ready.
i18n: helix.{badge,ariaLabel,tooltip,askHelix,thinking} + helix.{refreshing,errorLabel,noOutput} + ai.common.errorUnknown
  (brand keys resolve to web-English fallback exactly as web t(key,default) default-value contract, and common.{offline,retry} +
  error.network.offlineDetail (present in generated catalog). No English literals in code - all via StringResolver.
A11y: per-state merged TalkBack announcements (polite live region), Helix-badge merged label, contextual action
  content-description (Ask Helix - <verb>), long-press tooltips, reduced-motion-aware thinking affordance, Material 3 font scaling, minSdk 26.
Telemetry: view.opened emits surface slug 'AIFeatureCard' only (PII-safe, at most once).
Data binding: AIFeatureCardHost binds AIFeatureCardViewModel (P1/S8); reusable AIFeatureCard takes a host stream
  snapshot. No HTTP from the view. AiFeatureCardStreamSource is the native useAiStream seam.
Note: the prompt's allowed-files glob is the main surface dir; the mandated adapter/per-state/a11y tests live in
